{
 "id": "MAP-03",
 "name": "flight-tracker",
 "version": 1,
 "title": "A flight on a map",
 "summary": "The map building blocks in a canvas of their own: the North Atlantic from {\"$map\"} scaled uniformly and clipped, the airports from {\"$mapPoint\"}, the great-circle route from {\"$mapRoute\"}, the flown part as a pathExpression ending at the progress the app sends, and the plane at that fraction of the distance.",
 "prompt": "A flight tracker card: London to New York on a map, the plane along the route at the flight's progress, and the time left.",
 "level": 3,
 "family": "MAP",
 "capabilities": {
  "primary": [
   "map.marker",
   "map.region",
   "map.route"
  ],
  "secondary": [
   "draw.path",
   "host.variables",
   "text.dynamic",
   "data.expression"
  ]
 },
 "use_cases": [
  "map",
  "travel",
  "card"
 ],
 "form_factor": "phone",
 "keywords": [
  "delivery tracker map",
  "flight map",
  "flight path",
  "flight tracker",
  "great circle",
  "path between cities",
  "plane",
  "plane heading",
  "progress on a map",
  "route",
  "route on a map",
  "tracker map"
 ],
 "teaches": [
  "{\"$mapRoute\": {region, from, to}} is the great-circle path between two places; with \"axis\": \"x\" | \"y\" | \"angle\" it is the route's samples as a float array the document declares, and \"wrap\": \"arraySpline({}, @progress)\" the point at that fraction of the distance",
  "The flown part is a pathExpression over the same samples (arraySpline(..., a[0])) whose end is the host progress",
  "{\"$map\"} with a [lonMin, latMin, lonMax, latMax] region is a box 1000 wide and {\"$mapHeight\"} tall: scale it by ONE factor, min(componentWidth() / 1000, componentHeight() / height), centre it and clipRect it, or it stretches",
  "{\"$mapPoint\"} in resources.variables gives a city's x and y as numbers when the document is built",
  "A canvas with {\"verticalWeight\": 1} takes the height left in the column; the map scaled by min(componentWidth() / 1000, componentHeight() / height) follows the window"
 ],
 "inputs": {
  "variables": {
   "progress": {
    "type": "float",
    "meaning": "Flight progress 0..1",
    "default": 0.42,
    "min": 0,
    "max": 1,
    "step": 0.01
   },
   "minutesLeft": {
    "type": "float",
    "meaning": "Minutes to arrival",
    "default": 238,
    "min": 0,
    "max": 600,
    "step": 1
   }
  },
  "clock": null,
  "touch": false
 },
 "check": {
  "describe": "The North Atlantic from 100°W to 20°E, not stretched; London and New York marked, the great-circle route arching north between them, the part flown in the primary colour up to the plane 42 % of the way; variables {progress: 0.9} puts it near New York; the header reads 03 h 58 left. The map canvas takes the height under the header (a vertical weight) and scales the North Atlantic box to fit.",
